            <ArticleTitle>Mild Decarboxylative C-H Alkylation: Computational Insights for Solvent-Robust Ruthenium(II) Domino Manifold.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>17449-17453</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1002/chem.201703680</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Computational studies on decarboxylative C-H alkenylations provided key insights into the solvent-robust nature of C-H activation/decarboxylation domino reactions. These properties were exploited for ruthenium(II)-catalyzed C-H alkylations by a decarboxylative process with ample scope under copper-free and silver-free reaction conditions.</AbstractText>
